export const termsOfService = "# Terms of Service\n\n**Last updated:** October 24, 2026\n\nThese Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of the Haiku generation service (the website, application, and related features we offer). By using the Haiku generation service, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Haiku generation service.\n\nWe may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will revise the “Last updated” date above. Material changes may be communicated through the Haiku generation service or by email where appropriate. Continued use after changes take effect means you accept the updated Terms.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Haiku generation service\n\nThe Haiku generation service is a web-based tool that provides software features and related functionality as described on our site at the time you use it. We may add, change, or remove features to improve the product, maintain security, or comply with requirements we consider necessary.\n\nThe Haiku generation service is operated by an independent developer. It is not offered as a substitute for professional advice (legal, medical, financial, or otherwise). Outputs or results from any automated or AI-related features are for your convenience only; you remain responsible for how you use them.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Eligibility and your account\n\nYou must be able to enter a binding agreement to use the Haiku generation service. If you use the Haiku generation service on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that organization to these Terms.\n\nYou are responsible for:\n\n- Providing accurate information when required\n- Keeping any login credentials secure\n- All activity under your account\n\nNotify us promptly if you suspect unauthorized access.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Acceptable use\n\nYou agree not to:\n\n- Violate applicable law or infringe others’ rights\n- Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Haiku generation service, other users’ data, or our systems\n- Interfere with or disrupt the Haiku generation service (including by introducing malware or excessive automated load)\n- Reverse engineer, scrape, or misuse the Haiku generation service except where applicable law expressly permits and cannot be waived\n- Use the Haiku generation service to generate or distribute unlawful, harmful, or abusive content, or to harass others\n\nWe may suspend or terminate access if we reasonably believe you have breached these Terms or pose a risk to the Haiku generation service or other users.\n\nA standalone summary of these rules is in our [Acceptable Use Policy](/acceptable-use).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Payments and billing\n\n**Processor.** Payments for one-time purchases of credits are processed by **Paddle**, our payment provider. Paddle acts as the **merchant of record** for those transactions. That means Paddle handles checkout, payment collection, and certain tax and compliance obligations associated with the sale, as described in Paddle’s terms and policies at checkout.\n\n**Prices and taxes.** Prices are shown before you complete a purchase. Taxes, currency, and invoicing may be handled according to Paddle’s checkout and your location.\n\n**No subscriptions.** We currently sell one-time credit packs only (100 haiku generations for USD 3.00, plus applicable tax). Nothing renews automatically and there are no recurring charges.\n\n**Refunds.** Refund eligibility is governed by the refund and cancellation terms presented at purchase and by Paddle’s applicable policies. Where we offer a refund in line with those terms, Paddle may process it on our behalf.\n\n**Failed payments.** We or Paddle may suspend or downgrade access if a payment fails until the issue is resolved.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Intellectual property\n\nThe Haiku generation service, its branding, and its content (excluding content you provide) are owned by us or our licensors and are protected by intellectual property laws. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the Haiku generation service for your own purposes in line with these Terms.\n\nYou retain rights in content you submit. You grant us a license to host, process, and display that content only as needed to operate and improve the Haiku generation service for you, and as described in our privacy practices.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Third-party services\n\nThe Haiku generation service may rely on third parties (including Paddle and infrastructure providers). Their services are subject to their own terms. We are not responsible for third-party services we do not control.\n\n---\n\n## 7. No warranties\n\n**The Haiku generation service is provided “as is” and “as available.”** To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, we disclaim all warranties, whether express, implied, or statutory, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.\n\nWe do not warrant that the Haiku generation service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful components, or that any result or output will be accurate or suitable for your needs.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Limitation of liability\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by applicable law:\n\n- We are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for loss of profits, data, goodwill, or business opportunities, arising from your use of or inability to use the Haiku generation service.\n- Our total liability for any claim arising out of or relating to the Haiku generation service or these Terms is limited to the greater of **(a)** the amount you paid us for the Haiku generation service in the **twelve (12) months** before the event giving rise to the claim, or **(b)** **fifty U.S. dollars (USD 50)** if you have not paid anything in that period.\n\nSome jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations; in those cases, our liability is limited to the maximum permitted.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Indemnity\n\nYou agree to defend and indemnify us against claims, damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the Haiku generation service, your content, or your breach of these Terms, except to the extent caused by our intentional misconduct.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Termination\n\nYou may stop using the Haiku generation service at any time. We may suspend or terminate your access if you violate these Terms, if we must do so for legal or security reasons, or if we wind down or materially change the Haiku generation service.\n\nUpon termination, your right to use the Haiku generation service ends. Provisions that by their nature should survive (including payment obligations accrued before termination, intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability, and governing interpretations) will survive.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Changes to the Haiku generation service and to these Terms\n\nWe may modify or discontinue parts of the Haiku generation service. We may update these Terms as described at the top of this page. If you do not agree to an update, you should stop using the Haiku generation service.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Contact\n\nQuestions about these Terms or the Haiku generation service: email [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party). We aim to respond within a reasonable time.\n";

export const privacyPolicy = "# Privacy Policy\n\n**Last updated:** October 24, 2026\n\nThis Privacy Policy describes how we handle personal information when you use the Haiku generation service (the site, app, and related features). We keep collection limited to what we need to run the product, support accounts, and understand usage at a basic level.\n\nIf you do not agree with this Policy, please do not use the Haiku generation service.\n\nWe may update this Policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the “Last updated” date above. For meaningful changes, we may also notify you through the Haiku generation service or by email where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Who we are\n\nThe Haiku generation service is operated by an independent developer. For privacy requests, use the contact method described at the end of this Policy.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What information we collect\n\n**Account and authentication.** If you sign up or log in, we typically collect information such as your email address, and data needed to maintain your session or verify your identity (for example, tokens or identifiers associated with your account). If you use a third-party sign-in provider, we receive whatever profile details that provider shares with us according to your choices and their policies.\n\n**Usage and technical data.** We may collect basic information about how you use the Haiku generation service, such as pages or features accessed, approximate timestamps, and diagnostic data that helps us fix errors or improve performance. This is generally aggregated or logged at a level that supports operations rather than detailed profiling.\n\n**Content you provide.** If you submit text, preferences, or other content to the Haiku generation service, we store and process it as needed to provide the features you use.\n\n**Payments.** We do not receive or store your full payment card details on our own systems. Purchases are processed by **Paddle**, which acts as **merchant of record**. Paddle collects payment information and billing details required to complete a transaction. We may receive limited information from Paddle or from our own records, such as whether a purchase succeeded, product or plan identifiers, and enough detail to provide access you paid for.\n\n**Communications.** If you contact us, we keep the content of your message and related metadata (such as your email address) so we can respond.\n\nWe do not intentionally collect sensitive categories of data (such as health information) as part of the Haiku generation service. Please do not send us such information unless a feature explicitly requires it and we describe that separately.\n\n---\n\n## 3. How we use information\n\nWe use the information above to:\n\n- Provide, maintain, and improve the Haiku generation service  \n- Authenticate users and protect accounts  \n- Process transactions and manage access tied to purchases  \n- Send service-related messages (such as security notices, receipts, or responses to support)  \n- Understand aggregate or basic usage patterns and fix technical issues  \n- Comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms  \n\nWe do not sell your personal information. We do not use your data to build aggressive cross-site advertising profiles through our own product.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Legal bases (where they apply)\n\nDepending on where you live, laws such as the GDPR may require a “legal basis” for certain processing. In those cases, we generally rely on one or more of the following as appropriate: performing our contract with you (providing the Haiku generation service), legitimate interests that are not overridden by your rights (for example, securing the service and improving reliability), your consent where we ask for it, or compliance with legal obligations.\n\nThis Policy is not a complete legal analysis of every jurisdiction. If you have questions about how this applies to you, you may contact us using the details below.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Third-party services\n\nWe use service providers that help us run the Haiku generation service. They process information on our behalf according to their roles and their own terms and privacy notices. Examples may include:\n\n- **Paddle** — payment processing and related checkout, tax, and invoicing as merchant of record  \n- **Hosting, email, and infrastructure** — storing data and delivering the application  \n- **Authentication providers** — if you choose to sign in through a third party  \n- **Analytics** — basic measurement of traffic or product usage, configured to stay proportionate to our needs  \n\nWe encourage you to read the privacy policies of providers you interact with directly (especially at checkout with Paddle).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Cookies and similar technologies\n\nWe may use cookies, local storage, or similar technologies to keep you signed in, remember preferences, protect against abuse, and support basic analytics. You can control many cookies through your browser settings; blocking some cookies may limit certain features (for example, staying logged in).\n\nWe do not use cookies in complicated or hidden ways beyond what is typical for a small authenticated web application and proportionate analytics.\n\nFor a dedicated overview, see our [Cookie Policy](/cookies).\n\n---\n\n## 7. How long we keep information\n\nWe retain information only as long as needed for the purposes described in this Policy, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law (for example, tax or accounting records handled by Paddle or our tools). When data is no longer needed, we delete or anonymize it where feasible, subject to technical limits and backups.\n\nExact retention periods can vary by data type and legal context; if you want more detail about your own data, contact us.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Your choices and rights\n\nDepending on where you live, you may have rights to:\n\n- **Access** a copy of the personal information we hold about you  \n- **Correct** information that is inaccurate  \n- **Delete** certain information, subject to legal exceptions  \n- **Object** or **restrict** certain processing, where applicable  \n- **Withdraw consent** where processing is based on consent  \n- **Lodge a complaint** with a data protection authority in your region  \n\nTo exercise these rights, contact us using the method at the end of this Policy. We will respond within a reasonable time. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.\n\nIf you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or similar regions, you may have specific statutory rights; we aim to honor reasonable requests in line with applicable law. Nothing in this Policy promises a particular legal outcome in every case.\n\n---\n\n## 9. International transfers\n\nWe may process or store information in countries other than where you live. Where required, we use appropriate safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses offered by providers) as made available by our vendors. Details depend on our infrastructure choices over time.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Security\n\nWe take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, loss, or misuse. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure; we cannot guarantee absolute security.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Children\n\nThe Haiku generation service is not directed at children under the age where parental consent is required for online services in their region. We do not knowingly collect personal information from those children. If you believe we have done so, please contact us and we will take appropriate steps to delete the information.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Contact\n\nFor privacy questions or requests about your personal information, email [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party). We aim to respond within a reasonable time.\n\n---\n\n*This Policy is provided for transparency. It does not constitute legal advice, and it is not a certification of compliance with any specific law.*\n";

export const refundPolicy = "# Refund Policy\n\n**Last updated:** October 24, 2026\n\nThis Refund Policy explains how refunds work for the Haiku generation service. We try to be fair while keeping things sustainable for a small, low-cost product.\n\n**Billing is processed by Paddle**, our payment provider and **merchant of record**. Paddle collects payment, applies taxes where applicable, and handles checkout. Some refund steps may go through Paddle’s systems or policies; we work within that framework.\n\n---\n\n## 1. General approach\n\nDigital credits are easy to use right away. Because of that, **we generally do not offer refunds** once you have **used** the Haiku generation service in a way that consumed what you paid for—for example, after you have actively used paid features or redeemed credits.\n\nThis isn’t meant to be harsh; it reflects that the product is inexpensive, run by a solo developer, and costs real time and infrastructure to operate. We still want to fix real mistakes and genuine problems (see below).\n\n---\n\n## 2. When we may refund or credit\n\nWe may offer a **refund, partial refund, or account credit** when something is clearly wrong on our side or with billing, such as:\n\n- **Duplicate charge** for the same product or period  \n- **Technical failure** that prevented you from using what you paid for for a meaningful period, and we could not reasonably fix it in time  \n- **Billing error** (for example, you were charged the wrong amount)  \n- **Other exceptional cases** we judge in good faith—usually rare, and decided case by case  \n\nWe **do not** guarantee a refund in every situation. Each request is reviewed on its facts.\n\n---\n\n## 3. No subscriptions\n\nThe Haiku generation service currently sells **one-time credit packs only** (100 haiku generations for **USD 3.00**, plus applicable tax). There are **no subscriptions or recurring charges**, so there is nothing to cancel and you will never be billed again unless you choose to buy another pack.\n\n---\n\n## 4. One-time credit purchases\n\nCredits are **consumed when you use** features that spend them. **Purchased credits are not refundable** after they have been used, except where section 2 applies (e.g. duplicate charge or a serious technical issue that blocked use).\n\nIf credits were **never usable** due to a fault on our side and we confirm that, we will work with you on a reasonable fix, which may include restoring credits or a refund where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n## 5. How to request a refund or billing help\n\n1. **Contact us** at [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party). Include your account email, approximate date of charge, and a short description of the issue.  \n2. If Paddle sent you a receipt or customer portal link, you can also **check Paddle’s buyer support** for payment-specific questions; as merchant of record, Paddle may handle certain requests directly.  \n\nWe aim to reply within a **reasonable time**. Complex cases may take a bit longer. If we approve a refund, it is usually processed back through the original payment method, subject to Paddle’s and your bank’s processing times.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Chargebacks\n\nIf you have a problem, please **contact us first** so we can try to resolve it. Unnecessary chargebacks can lead to account restrictions and make it harder to help you quickly.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Changes\n\nWe may update this Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do. Continued use of paid features after updates means you accept the revised Policy for new purchases.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Contact\n\nFor refund or billing questions, email [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party). We will do our best to be helpful and clear.\n";

export const cookiePolicy = "# Cookie Policy\n\n**Last updated:** October 24, 2026\n\nThis Cookie Policy explains how the Haiku generation service uses cookies and similar technologies. It is a short companion to our [Privacy Policy](/privacy), which has more detail on personal data overall.\n\n---\n\n## What cookies and similar technologies are\n\nCookies are small text files stored on your device. We also use similar technologies where relevant, such as **local storage** for preferences or session-related data in the browser.\n\n---\n\n## How we use them\n\n**Essential / functional.** We use cookies or storage as needed to run the Haiku generation service—for example, to keep you signed in, protect against abuse, remember UI choices, or route traffic securely. These are not used for advertising on our site.\n\n**Analytics.** We may use limited, privacy-conscious analytics to understand aggregate usage (such as which pages or features are used). We aim to keep this proportionate to operating a small product, not to build invasive profiles.\n\n**Payments.** When you pay, **Paddle** (our merchant of record) operates checkout. Paddle may set their own cookies or use similar technologies on their checkout pages or portals, under [Paddle’s privacy notice](https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy) and the terms shown at purchase.\n\n---\n\n## Your choices\n\nYou can control cookies through your browser settings. Blocking or deleting **essential** cookies may mean some features stop working—for example, you may need to sign in again more often.\n\nFor analytics, if we offer a simple opt-out or use a provider with industry opt-out tools, we will describe that in the app or update this page when relevant.\n\n---\n\n## Updates\n\nWe may update this Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date above will change when we do.\n\n---\n\n## Contact\n\nQuestions: email [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party), or see the [Privacy Policy](/privacy) for more on your rights and our practices.\n";

export const acceptableUsePolicy = "# Acceptable Use Policy\n\n**Last updated:** October 24, 2026\n\nThis Acceptable Use Policy (“AUP”) sets out rules for using the Haiku generation service. It is part of how we keep the product workable for everyone. The [Terms of Service](/terms) also apply, including for enforcement.\n\n---\n\n## Allowed use\n\nUse the Haiku generation service only for lawful purposes and in line with our Terms. Personal, hobby, and reasonable commercial use are fine unless we say otherwise for a specific plan or feature.\n\n---\n\n## Prohibited conduct\n\nYou must not:\n\n- Break the law or violate anyone else’s rights  \n- Try to access accounts, data, or systems you are not authorized to use  \n- Disrupt or overload the Haiku generation service (including malware, aggressive scraping, or attempts to bypass limits or security)  \n- Reverse engineer or misuse the Haiku generation service beyond what the law allows and we cannot contract out of  \n- Use the Haiku generation service to create or spread unlawful, harmful, abusive, or harassing content  \n- Impersonate others or misrepresent your affiliation  \n- Use the Haiku generation service to send spam or unsolicited bulk communications through our features  \n\n---\n\n## Enforcement\n\nWe may warn you, suspend access, or close accounts if we reasonably believe you have breached this AUP or the Terms, or if you create risk for the Haiku generation service or other people. We try to be fair and proportionate; serious or repeated issues may lead to immediate termination.\n\n---\n\n## Reporting\n\nIf you see abuse tied to the Haiku generation service, email [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party). We cannot promise a specific outcome for every report, but we review genuine issues.\n\n---\n\n## Changes\n\nWe may update this AUP from time to time. The “Last updated” date will change when we do. Continued use after updates means you accept the revised AUP for ongoing use.\n\n---\n\n## Contact\n\nQuestions about this policy: email [support@gpderp.party](mailto:support@gpderp.party).\n";
